apitrace: a headless eglretrace, for Android and the desktop

A replay that measures a GL implementation must not be paced by anything
else, and must run where no window system is: every drawable a pbuffer,
EGL from EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY, nothing to open and nothing to present to.
Upstream's eglretrace opens an X display even with --headless, and on a
desktop driver its swaps then present to that display and wait for the
compositor. glws_egl_headless.cpp is glws_egl_xlib.cpp with X11 removed;
it is built as eglretrace-headless beside the X11 eglretrace, and as the
eglretrace on Android, which upstream dropped. There glproc_egl.cpp loads
the unversioned library names and takes GL entry points from the
eglGetProcAddress of the libEGL the binary links - which a libEGL.so placed
first on LD_LIBRARY_PATH (the shim in front of the wrapper) answers instead
of the driver's. The CMake changes build the Android target with the
bundled third-party libraries. Applies on top of
apitrace-glcalllists-remap.patch.

